{"title":"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">2025 AMC 10B #8</a> and <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2025 AMC 12B #6</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Trial_and_Error)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Trial and Error)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:15)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:15)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Emmy says to Max, \"I ordered <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> math club sweatshirts today.\" Max asks, \"How much did each shirt cost?\" Emmy responds, \"I'll give you a hint. The total cost was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/3/f53b76857c7bd6e712912e818459f4f0d68762d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$ \\underline A~\\underline B~\\underline B.\\underline B~\\underline A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"19\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are digits and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/1/9f1b1aa227a453a609e4ca3689c5f75312233756.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" />.\" After a pause, Max says, \"That was a good price.\" What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5bf77c6740d00af2866f26718d628a60c667ef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/0/080cadba56a49af543d986b8eef417de10305ab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~7 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}~8 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}~11 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}~14 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}~15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"378\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The problem is essentially telling us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/3/373e474f48a43d5244e984b704153034f0c57404.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline A~\\underline B~\\underline B.\\underline B~\\underline A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so it is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Then, by the divisibility by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> condition,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/7/717a84b3866daf898abe4ce8c735776d79a9102f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A+B+B+B+A=2A+3B\\equiv 0\\pmod{9}\\]\" width=\"366\" height=\"18\" />\nThis means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or otherwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/e/fae80bd40963c204d0591a739a266bbde33d3965.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2A+3B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" /> would not be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/4/d948e33806532ca5e2287afb989211ae5f1380d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A\\ne0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" />, we must have one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/2/0f24a577c2ebdca302ae97fb069cb0f63d76ebb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=3,6,9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> must be even or else the entire number would not be even and thus would not be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af04466ac38b7b0d0f451b3280c38f861ea13822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/5/2152c10349e2a885a74b15e7097dd178b9b97f06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 6+3B\\equiv 0\\pmod{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"185\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/1/c516fc49de8fe7e12c688c7365962b27e7e7565a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+B\\equiv 0\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"20\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/7/18764e7bbf827415a5cc9f64a15aed17e613cd37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B\\equiv 2\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"20\" />. This yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/7/6074b666713ad941d6f2f3aaa7e226544e442efa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=2,5,8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />, of which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/3/9d37c9db717a59347ab04a8815c71fa1fbaa9c2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> is the only number that allows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/3/373e474f48a43d5244e984b704153034f0c57404.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline A~\\underline B~\\underline B.\\underline B~\\underline A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> to be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/d/43dc50110aad5478016314fe319896abfcd1527a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+5=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}~11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"130\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~ <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Eevee9406\">eevee9406</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Trial_and_Error.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Trial_and_Error)\">Solution 2 (Trial and Error)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Trial and Error)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A number is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> if it divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The divisibility rule for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> requires the last 2 digits to also be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The divisibility rule for 9 requires the sum of all digits to be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Using the first condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b831312585cb4ab6697896f86b72accbddbc4b45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> is a multiple of 4. We can list out all possibilities for this, since both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are digits. The possibilities are  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb183dedd20cbc63f6025eb8a17ec4580b233930.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,2),(1,6),...(9,6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. There are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> digits that are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />'s and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />'s. So if the digits sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/e/fae80bd40963c204d0591a739a266bbde33d3965.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2A+3B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" /> is a multiple of 9. We can try plugging in numbers from our list earlier into the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/e/fae80bd40963c204d0591a739a266bbde33d3965.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2A+3B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" /> to find what values set the expression equal to a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. By trying numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af04466ac38b7b0d0f451b3280c38f861ea13822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/3/9d37c9db717a59347ab04a8815c71fa1fbaa9c2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />. So then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b831312585cb4ab6697896f86b72accbddbc4b45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> yields \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/d/43dc50110aad5478016314fe319896abfcd1527a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+5=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}~11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"130\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~NumberNinja1234\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E1:15.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:15)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:15)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:15)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/MI8-1uFfzKU\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/MI8-1uFfzKU</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/vayQuXXbr28\">https://youtu.be/vayQuXXbr28</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Quick_and_Simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Quick and Simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=161_NNdnBtU\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=161_NNdnBtU</a>\n~Sigma_Bob\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Fast_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy)\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Fast and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q5b3VjAsglU\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q5b3VjAsglU</a>\n</p><p>~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLSWVrrKsgs\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLSWVrrKsgs</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B\" title=\"2025 AMC 10B\">2025 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2025 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><